<title>ITALY: Breakdown of deficit cuts in Italian mini-budget.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of deficit cuts in Italian mini-budget.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the measures included in the Italian mini-budget, which was approved on Thursday by the cabinet, and how they will raise revenue over the next three years.</p>
<p>(Figures in billions of lire)</p>
<p>				    1997	 1998	 1999</p>
<p>Advance tax on severance</p>
<p>  payment funds		6,000	6,200	  250</p>
<p>Delayed payments of</p>
<p>severance handouts to</p>
<p>  state workers		2,600	  200	  200</p>
<p>Tax amnesty on social</p>
<p>  security payments	    400	  200	  200</p>
<p>Elimination of forward</p>
<p>payment on building</p>
<p>  contracts			500	  200	   --</p>
<p> Ministry spending cuts    1,300	   --	   --</p>
<p>Changing status of full</p>
<p>time state workers to</p>
<p>  part-time.			--	   30	    50</p>
<p>Sale of buildings owned</p>
<p>  by state bodies		 --	1,000	 1,500</p>
<p>Elimination of credits</p>
<p>  to state bodies		 --	  100	   200</p>
<p> Rise in postal tariffs	500	  600	   700</p>
<p> Fiscal measures	     4,200	2,000	 2,000</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> TOTAL			  15,500     10,530	 5,100</p>
<p>Note - The fiscal measures include simplifying procedures for payment of inheritance tax and seeking advance payment of certain types of tax. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
